.TH TRICKLED 8 "October 2026" "ntrickle 2.0.0" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
trickled \- ntrickle coordination daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B trickled
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B trickled
coordinates bandwidth grants for wrapped processes.  It listens on a Unix
domain socket, verifies client credentials with the kernel, applies the
two-tier weight-proportional scheduler, per-user caps, process overrides, and
time-based schedules, and serves a JSON control socket for
.B trickle top
and
.BR "trickle stats" .
.PP
The installed command is
.BR trickled ;
.B ntrickled
is an optional alias for the same daemon.  The daemon runs in the foreground
by default.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-v, \-\-verbose
Increase logging verbosity.  May be repeated.
.TP
.B \-D, \-\-daemonize
Fork and detach from the terminal.
.TP
.B \-\-log-file \fIFILE\fR
Append log output to
.IR FILE .
.TP
.B \-d, \-\-download-rate \fIRATE\fR
Set the global download limit.  A unit is required, for example
.BR 100M ,
.BR 1G ,
or
.BR unlimited .
The default is 100M.
.TP
.B \-u, \-\-upload-rate \fIRATE\fR
Set the global upload limit, using the same syntax as
.BR \-d .
.TP
.B \-t, \-\-time-smooth \fISECONDS\fR
Set the default smoothing time.  The default is 3.0.
.TP
.B \-l, \-\-length-smooth \fIKB\fR
Set the default smoothing length.  The default is 20.
.TP
.B \-W, \-\-weight \fIN\fR
Set the default process weight.  The minimum is 1.
.TP
.B \-\-idle-threshold \fISECONDS\fR
Idle threshold for dynamic fairness.  The default is 3.
.TP
.B \-\-burst \fISECONDS\fR
Burst duration for new connections.  The default is 0 (disabled); set a
positive value to enable burst mode.
.TP
.B \-\-burst-bandwidth \fIRATE\fR
Bandwidth during the burst window.  The default is
.BR unlimited .
.TP
.B \-c, \-\-config \fIFILE\fR
Read the TOML daemon configuration from
.IR FILE .
.TP
.B \-n, \-\-socket \fIPATH\fR
Use
.IR PATH
as the data socket.  The control socket is
.IR PATH .ctl
and the lock file is
.IR PATH .lock.
.TP
.B \-N, \-\-notify \fISECONDS\fR
Log aggregate bandwidth usage every
.I SECONDS
seconds.  The default is 0 (disabled).
.TP
.B \-F, \-\-fairness \fIMODE\fR
Select
.B static
or
.B dynamic
fairness.  The default is
.BR static .
.TP
.B \-w, \-\-window \fIKB\fR
Set the peak-detection window in kilobytes.  The default is 200.
.TP
.B \-\-schedules \fIPATH\fR
Use the specified schedules file.
.TP
.B \-\-process-config \fIPATH\fR
Use the specified process configuration file.
.TP
.B \-\-suppress-warnings
Suppress schedule-collision warnings.
.TP
.B \-V, \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Print help and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/ntrickle/ntrickled.toml
Daemon configuration.
.TP
.I /etc/ntrickle/process.toml
Per-process overrides.
.TP
.I /etc/ntrickle/schedules.toml
Time-based overrides.
.TP
.I /run/ntrickle/ntrickled.sock
Default data socket.
.SH COMPATIBILITY
This is the modern ntrickle daemon.  Classic
.B trickled
options such as
.BR \-f ,
.BR \-s ,
and
.BR \-p ,
the
.I /etc/trickled.conf
format, the
.I /tmp/.trickled.sock
socket, and the classic wire protocol are not supported.  The daemon is
foreground by default; use
.B \-D
only when a daemonizing process is required.  See
.I docs/compatibility.md
and
.I docs/migration-classic.md
in the source distribution.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR trickle (1)
